WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.451
PII and consent.

2
00:00:01.731 --> 00:00:07.768
Training data deserves more care than prompt data, for a technical reason: models can memorize it.

3
00:00:08.048 --> 00:00:24.005
Carlini and colleagues (2021) extracted hundreds of verbatim training sequences from GPT-2, including names, phone numbers, and email addresses, and some of those sequences appeared in only one document in the training data.

4
00:00:24.285 --> 00:00:26.419
Larger models were more vulnerable.

5
00:00:26.699 --> 00:00:37.899
A fine-tuned model is trained on far less data, but it is also trained for several epochs on exactly your examples, which is the condition under which memorization is easiest.

6
00:00:38.179 --> 00:00:43.896
Assume a fine-tuned model can repeat pieces of its training set to anyone who can query it.

7
00:00:44.176 --> 00:00:46.245
Four habits follow: Minimize.

8
00:00:46.525 --> 00:00:55.763
If the task doesn’t need the customer’s name, account number, or address to learn the behavior, remove or replace it before the data reaches the training set.

9
00:00:56.043 --> 00:01:04.917
Tools such as Presidio (open source) detect and mask many common PII types; measure what it misses on your data before relying on it.

10
00:01:05.197 --> 00:01:06.563
Consent and purpose.

11
00:01:06.843 --> 00:01:12.048
Data collected to resolve a support ticket wasn’t necessarily collected to train a model.

12
00:01:12.328 --> 00:01:18.301
Whether you may reuse it depends on your contracts, privacy notices, and the law where your users live.

13
00:01:18.581 --> 00:01:24.875
That is a question for your privacy and legal teams, and the answer belongs in the dataset’s documentation.

14
00:01:25.155 --> 00:01:26.029
Deletion.

15
00:01:26.309 --> 00:01:33.264
When a person asks for their data to be deleted, you can delete a row from a file, but you can’t delete it from trained weights.

16
00:01:33.544 --> 00:01:41.480
The practical answer is to retrain from the corrected data, so keep the pipeline that rebuilds the dataset and the model reproducible.

17
00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:42.635
Access.

18
00:01:42.915 --> 00:01:46.520
A training file is a concentrated copy of sensitive data.

19
00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:49.957
Store it like production data, not in a notebook folder.

20
00:01:50.237 --> 00:01:53.480
The lab’s data is entirely fictional, with reserved.

21
00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:57.749
example email domains, so you can practice without any of these risks.

22
00:01:58.029 --> 00:02:00.653
Real projects start with the questions above.
